  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the sum of the measures of the six minor arcs on the circumcircle of triangle \\( \\triangle DEF \\), given that the points \\( G, D, E, H, J, \\) and \\( F \\) divide the circumcircle into these arcs.\n\nFirst, we need to understand the properties of the triangle and the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\). The circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) has its center at the circumcenter of \\( \\triangle DEF \\). The angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) are half of the angles of \\( \\triangle ABC \\) because \\( D, E, \\) and \\( F \\) are the midpoints of \\( \\triangle ABC \\).\n\nThe angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) are:\n\\[\n\\angle D = \\angle BAC / 2 = 84^\\circ / 2 = 42^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle E = \\angle ABC / 2 = 60^\\circ / 2 = 30^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle F = \\angle ACB / 2 = 36^\\circ / 2 = 18^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the angles in a triangle is \\( 180^\\circ \\), so the sum of the angles in \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is:\n\\[\n42^\\circ + 30^\\circ + 18^\\circ = 90^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSince \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is a triangle, the sum of the angles in \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is \\( 180^\\circ \\). The sum of the angles around the center of the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is \\( 360^\\circ \\). The angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) are the central angles corresponding to the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\).\n\nThe sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is \\( 360^\\circ \\). The sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is also equal to the sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DG}, \\widehat{GH}, \\widehat{HE}, \\widehat{EH}, \\widehat{HF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FG} \\).\n\nSince the sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is \\( 360^\\circ \\), we can find the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) by considering the properties of the triangle and the circumcircle.\n\nThe measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) are:\n\\[\n\\widehat{DE} = 180^\\circ - \\angle D = 180^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 138^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\widehat{EF} = 180^\\circ - \\angle E = 180^\\circ - 30^\\circ = 150^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\widehat{FD} = 180^\\circ - \\angle F = 180^\\circ - 18^\\circ = 162^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is:\n\\[\n138^\\circ + 150^\\circ + 162^\\circ = 450^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is also equal to the sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DG}, \\widehat{GH}, \\widehat{HE}, \\widehat{EH}, \\widehat{HF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FG} \\).\n\nThe sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DG}, \\widehat{GH}, \\widehat{HE}, \\widehat{EH}, \\widehat{HF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FG} \\) is:\n\\[\n450^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the measures of the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE}, \\widehat{EF}, \\) and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) is:\n\\[\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 138^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 150^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 162^\\circ = 138^\\circ + 300^\\circ + 486^\\circ = 924^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{924}.\n\\]",
